<section class="wrap surveillance-questions">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Design backward from the question</p>
    <h2>A camera on the wall is not the same as a usable image.</h2>
    <p>Placement, height, distance, lighting, and the expected moment all change what a camera can help you understand.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="surveillance-question-grid">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Who arrived?</h3><p>Plan entry and approach views around people entering and leaving the property.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>What happened here?</h3><p>Match the view to the customer, work, counter, or storage area that matters.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Which direction?</h3><p>Use exterior sightlines to understand movement across parking and perimeter areas.</p></article>
    <article><span>04</span><h3>When did it happen?</h3><p>Organize recording and review around a workflow your team can actually use.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

